TEST_DESCRIPTION
The Delete Payload contains a protocol-specific security association
identifier that the sender has removed from its security association
(Tests that DUT sends delete payloads for all the SA removed from its
Database)
TEST_REFERENCE
RFC 2408 s3.15 p41 Delete Payload
TEST_METHOD
- ANVL: Establish one ISAKMP SA with DUT
- ANVL: Externally cause DUT to initiate an IPSEC SA for ESP
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(1),SA1,Ni,KE>
   - ANVL: Send <HDR*,HASH(2),SA1,Nr,KE>
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(3)>
- ANVL: Externally cause DUT to initiate another IPSEC SA for ESP
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(1),SA2,Ni,KE>
   - ANVL: Send <HDR*,HASH(2),SA2,Nr,KE>
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(3)>
- ANVL: Externally cause DUT to delete both IPSEC SAs
-  DUT: Send one <HDR*,DEL> with 2 SPIs for the 2 deleted SAs or
        2 <HDR*,DEL> for each of the deleted SAs
TEST_CLASSIFICATION
MUST
TEST_TOPOLOGY
TOPOLOGY-0

