TEST_DESCRIPTION
A single SA negotiation results in two security assocations--
one inbound and one outbound. In either case, "SPI" from
the ISAKMP Proposal Payload that contained the negotiated
Transform.
The SPI value of zero (0) is reserved for local,
implementation-specific use and MUST NOT be sent on the wire.
Quick mode/DUT initiated/Negative
TEST_REFERENCE
NEGATIVE: RFC 2408 s4.2 p48 Security Association Establishment
          RFC 2406 s2.1 p4 Security Parameters Index
          RFC 2409 s5.5 p18 Phase 2 - Quick Mode
TEST_METHOD
- ANVL: Establish one ISAKMP SA with DUT
- ANVL: Externally cause DUT to initiate one IPSEC SA
        containing 2 Proposals
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(1),SA,Ni,KE> Packet
- ANVL: Send <HDR*,HASH(2),SA,Nr,KE> Packet with SPI
        field in Proposal Payload set to local reserved value (0)
-  DUT: Do not send <HDR*,HASH(3)> packet
TEST_CLASSIFICATION
MUST
TEST_TOPOLOGY
TOPOLOGY-0

