<< IKE-23.2: Passed

>> IKE-23.3
TEST_DESCRIPTION
It is observed in some IKE daemon, that on receipt of an
unauthorized delete message, they delete all IPsec SAs pointing
to the source IP address of the ISAKMP message if the ISAKMP
message originates from the right IP address
(An attacker can inject the delete packet after sending a Main mode
<HDR, SA> packets to the network. It is to check if DUT is robust
enough to detect that)
TEST_REFERENCE
Web ref: http://securityfocus.com/archive/1/348637
RFC 2408 s5.5 p63 Proposal Payload Processing
TEST_METHOD
- ANVL: Establish an ISAKMP SA with DUT
- ANVL: Establish an IPSec SA with DUT
- ANVL: Send a ICMP Echo Request from Local Host
-  DUT: Forward the secured ICMP Echo Request to Remote Host
- ANVL: As an attacker send <HDR, SA> Packet
-  DUT: Send <HDR,SA> Packet
- ANVL: As an attacker send <HDR, HASH, DEL> Packet with dummy
        hash payload
- ANVL: As an attacker send another <HDR, DEL> Packet without
        hash payload
-  DUT: Do not delete the IPSec SA without proper authentication
        of the packet received
- ANVL: Send a ICMP Echo Request from Local Host
-  DUT: Forward the secured ICMP Echo Request to Remote Host
TEST_CLASSIFICATION
MUST
TEST_TOPOLOGY
TOPOLOGY-0

